%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d56cce9b854dbe4eb4d220d3699184f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Plot_C0_S1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Client::PlotConfig
  chapterId: 0
  sceneId: 1
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    text: Welcome to the combat tutorial
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: '<u>WASD</u> : move camera around.

      <u>Scroll your mouse</u>: zoom
      in/out/'
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Now we will learn the basic mechanics of the game.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: This is "instant", you can think of it as a fraction of time. A battle
      = 150 instants.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 60
  - type: 0
    text: 'It is just like an hour = 60 minutes, a second = 1000 miliseconds...

      Just
      different ways to calculate time, but all similar ideas.'
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'Now look at this bar over here: you can (and only can) command units that
      is on this bar when it''s your turn.'
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: And this bar is your opponent's bar, similar rule is applied.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_3
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Oh and when is your turn? Look over there, you can tell if the <u>Wait</u>
      button is visible.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: So yes, it is currently your turn. Click here to select your only available
      unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Perfect. On select a unit, you can select another <u>blue cell</u> as a
      target to move there. Click this cell first.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm your decision by clicking here.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 4
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Notice anything special? It is still your turn right?
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Dont worry, you are not breaking any rule. And the rule is really simple.
      Please look above, see the eyes? This is your eye.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_YourEye
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: And this is your opponent's eye. Notice the difference yet?
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_EnemyEye
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: So yes, this is a turn-based game. The most obvious rule is each side take
      turns sequentially. But if one side's eye is closed, then that side no longer
      takes any turn. Simple right?
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'Also you can rest assured: an eye will not re-open if the instant hasn''t
      passed. Look: its still the same <u>instant</u> isn''t it?'
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: But when will the eyes open again? => The next <u>paused instant</u> if
      that side has <u>ready unit</u>.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Then when is the next <u>paused instant</u>? => It is simple, after both
      sides closes the eyes, time flows again, and it will pause the <u>instant</u>
      when any new unit(s) enters the Ready Queue.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Too much to handle? Dont worry just hit the <u>Wait button</u> and follow
      the tutorial, you will understand soon enough.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 13
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'Alot happened right? Eyes closed, opened, then closed.... So brief explanation:
      the bot for this tutorial auto skips its turn, and you can feel free to explore
      the game mechanism. (this explain the nearst eye closing)'
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Ok now select a unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Here are your unit's information. Avoid getting HP to 0 is recommended.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_CharStat
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: These are your unit's skills.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Skills
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 2
    text: Right click (or hold) on any skill for detailed description.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: This is the skill description, all information on this panel is important,
      you will find out later.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_InspectPanel
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now let's click here to cancel (in fact you can click anywhere else).
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_CancelButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: "Now here is the fun part: you can decide to <u>Wait</u> even if you haven't
      commanded any unit. \nThis strategic decision can help you preserve units for
      the following <u>paused instants</u>."
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 12
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: NIce to meet you again, this time we'll get to the beautiful part of the
      game.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Notice you have 2 units in the <u>ready queue</u>? Thats right, one is
      reserved from the previous <u>paused instant (PI)</u>.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now select this unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Let's move to this cell.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: -2, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm the decision.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 3
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now select this unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 6
    text: Let's see what he can do. Select his main weapon skill.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Notice the blue cells? These cells are cells that he can attack from his
      position, memorize  this quickly. (move camera around if necessary)
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now we have to re-select him to select his movement skill. First click
      the cancel button.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_CancelButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Let's select him again.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: There are 2 cells that are suitable, the first one is this cell
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 2, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: This is the second suitable cell, let's choose this one, it is for something
      I want to show you later.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm the movement.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 3
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Perfect. Now select him again.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit2
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 6
    text: Select his main weapon skill.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Lock the target.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm the decision and focus here, the interesting part is about to come.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 1
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Hmm an aura appears, aside from that, nothing happened right?
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: To answer your questions, let's inspect the skill you commanded previously.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Oh right, he is not on the <u>Ready queue</u> anymore, see?
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_2
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Select him directly instead.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 2
    text: Inspect the skill.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'The skill description is simple isnt it? Attack the target... but it did
      not happen... has anything gone wrong? Actually, everything is working as designed. '
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_InspectPanel
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Look at this part, this is the skill type.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_STYPE
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'There are 3 types: Instant / HalfInstant / NonInstant.

      An example
      for <u>Instant skill</u> is the movement skill you have been using, it''s effect
      is applied immediately after you commanded.'
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'So the attack skill you just used, is the most simple example for <u>NonInstant</u>
      skill.

      How it works: time paused (eye(s) opens) -> commands -> both
      eyes closes -> non-instant skills that was commanded now takes effect -> time
      flows again.'
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: "So, to simplify this: \nIt is not <u>\"what you commanded did not happen\"
      </u>\nIt is <u>\"what you commanded has not happened yet\" </u>"
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Oh and by the way, the <u>NonInstant</u> skill command also immediately
      removes the unit from <u>Ready queue</u>.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now, for the skill to happen, click the wait button and watch
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_CancelButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now, for the skill to happen, click the wait button and watch
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 12
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Simple isn't it?
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Hmm last <u>paused instant</u> you commanded both units, but now only this
      one available, wonder why?
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_2
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Let's see... oh! There is a number, see?
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'For a simple explanation: because in the same <u>paused instant </u> ,
      the tank unit act faster (fewer commands), so he recovers faster. The calculation
      part is up to you, goodluck.'
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: For now, take it easy, you have been doing well.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: -2, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Let's setup for a final blow. Select this unit.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: -2, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Move to this cell.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Move to this cell.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 3
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Ok that's enough, let's save for the final blow.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 11
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Yes. We keep saving for the final blow, another wait please.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 10
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Alright, all our units are ready. Let's begin.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Select this unit first.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Move him to this cell.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 3
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Select him again.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 6
    text: Select his attack skill.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Select this cell to attack. No one is there? Haha don't worry, Im about
      to show you an interesting final blow.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: -1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm. Trust me, it will work.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 2, y: 1}
    delay: 2
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Now we select the last unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit1
    targetCell: {x: 2, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 2
    text: Inspect this skill, we will use this skill next.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_CSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 2, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: "Take your time, read it. \nHave you understand the plan? "
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_InspectPanel
    targetCell: {x: 2, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 3
    text: Select the only selectable target, according to our plan this is the suitable
      target (lol).
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm to continue.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 3
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Select the unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit1
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
  - type: 3
    text: Move to this cell.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: -1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 3
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
  - type: 1
    text: Select him again.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_Unit1
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
  - type: 6
    text: Now select his main attack skill.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: -1}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
  - type: 3
    text: Select the target.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WSKILL
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm and watch. This is the end of the tutorial, thankyou for participating,
      and hope to see you again.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 1, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 0.5
